<article class="env-example" id="04NB">
<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/04NB">Example <span data-tag="04NB">9.6.0.4</span>.</a> We have already encountered several examples of weak factorization systems $(S_{L}, S_{R} )$ on the category $\operatorname{Set_{\Delta }}$ of simplicial sets: </p>
<p><ul>
<li><p>
We can take $S_{R}$ to be the collection of Kan fibrations and $S_{L}$ the collection of anodyne morphisms (Proposition <a data-tag="00UV" href="/tag/00UV">3.1.8.1</a>). 
</p>
</li><li><p>
We can take $S_{R}$ to be the collection of inner fibrations and $S_{L}$ the collection of inner anodyne morphisms (Proposition <a data-tag="01BP" href="/tag/01BP">4.1.3.2</a>). 
</p>
</li><li><p>
We can take $S_{R}$ to be the collection of left fibrations and $S_{L}$ the collection of left anodyne morphisms (Proposition <a data-tag="014Z" href="/tag/014Z">4.2.4.7</a>). 
</p>
</li><li><p>
We can take $S_{R}$ to be the collection of right fibrations and $S_{L}$ the collection of right anodyne morphisms (Variant <a data-tag="0150" href="/tag/0150">4.2.4.8</a>). 
</p>
</li><li><p>
We can take $S_{R}$ to be the collection of trivial Kan fibrations and $S_{L}$ the collection of monomorphisms (Exercise <a data-tag="00UY" href="/tag/00UY">3.1.8.11</a>). 
</p>
</li>
</ul></p>
<p> Beware that none of these are factorization systems (in the sense of Definition <a data-tag="06VS" href="/tag/06VS">9.6.0.1</a>). </p>
</article>
